  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-05-28T22:16:38.352Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This would help creators who are commissioned to create avatars for newer/other players. As the only way to do that would be by either giving them a unity project in which they would still need to setup certain things or to share their account details with the creator. Which in turn is not a good idea.\n\nEssentially, adding an option when uploading an avatar to allow the creator to upload the avatar for a separate user. This can be done in a few ways in which the receiver can obtain a randomized code via the main site and within the Unity VRC SDK Menu, the creator can click the \"Upload to a different User\", and enter in the specific code that the receiver has obtained and then the avatar can be uploaded to the user, the code will expire within 15 minutes as well in order to prevent exploits. This in turn will bypass the need of sharing private account information and prevents others from randomly spamming others with avatar upload requests.",
